WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.690
When the economy slides into a recession,

2
00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:05.100
two different players can step in.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.390
Congress controls government
spending and taxes.

4
00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:10.230
That's fiscal policy.

5
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.470
The Fed controls the money supply
by buying and selling bonds.

6
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.370
That's monetary policy.

7
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.520
Sometimes they push the same way.

8
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.340
Sometimes they push in
opposite directions.

9
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.630
So why can the right cure for one slump

10
00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.920
be the wrong cure for the next?

11
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.290
In this mission, you'll see
what happens to real GDP,

12
00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:32.850
the price level and interest
rates when both act.

13
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.100
Then you'll mix the
two policies in a graph

14
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.000
lab and predict what
the interest rate does.

15
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.870
Your mission: find out how to
choose the right policy mix.
